{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeH3","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":34,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.unified_iterative_telescope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.unified_iterative_telescope","kind":"theorem","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L298-L303","doc":"Per-step contribution of the unified iterative correction telescopes:\n`Δ₂₂ · w₂₂ · (L_A - L_0) = Δ₂₂ · w₂₂ · L_A - Δ₂₂ · w₂₂ · L_0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.delta_22_q_hook","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.delta_22_q_hook","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L292-L296","doc":"The categorical Wigner / shell energy scale\n`Δ_(2,2) = m_e · H_q((2,2))` with `H_q((2,2)) = [3]_q · [2]_q²`: a\npurely algebraic product of `m_e` with the four hook q-integers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.categoricalResidualDetection_of_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.categoricalResidualDetection_of_neg","kind":"instance","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L276-L280","doc":"**Default instance from a strict-negativity hypothesis** (any `[Preorder α]`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.categoricalResidualDetection_of_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.categoricalResidualDetection_of_pos","kind":"instance","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L270-L274","doc":"**Default instance from a positivity hypothesis** (any `[Preorder α]`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.CategoricalResidualDetection.nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.CategoricalResidualDetection.nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L268-L268","doc":"The detected residual is non-zero (i.e. structure is informative). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.CategoricalResidualDetection.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.CategoricalResidualDetection.mk","kind":"ctor","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L265-L265","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.CategoricalResidualDetection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.CategoricalResidualDetection","kind":"class","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L257-L268","doc":"The general categorical process for detecting unpaired crossings via\nthe per-`(k, residual)` Wedderburn projection of the running NF\ntransition.  This class records that the `k`-th-level partition\nstructure detects a specific (non-zero) residual term.\n\nGeneric over any `[Zero α]` residual carrier (kept off `ℝ` so the\nfile's base-ring note holds — an ordered instantiation is only needed\nfor the default instances below). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.wigner_energy_from_22","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.wigner_energy_from_22","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L246-L255","doc":"The Wigner-energy term is `V_pn × α × Z / A` (per nucleon), with\n`V_pn = W_std · (z + dh)` the pn binding volume (§5).  The algebraic\ncontent is the commutativity/associativity rearrangement of that\nproduct (the `Z/A` normalisation is a common scalar factor and is not\npart of the identity), abstracting the pn binding volume as `v`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:wigner-np-pairing","label":"prop:wigner-np-pairing","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wigner-np-pairing.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.a3_extremal_cancel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.a3_extremal_cancel","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L235-L242","doc":"The a₃ formula for Z=N odd-odd nuclei with `sp = -ap` (extremal\ncancellation): `W_sym·sp + W_std·V_std + W_alt·(-sp) = W_std·V_std`\nwhen `W_sym = W_alt`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.a3_equal_characters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.a3_equal_characters","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L221-L233","doc":"The a₃ **numerator** for Z=N nuclei with all three characters equal\n(`sp = V_std = ap = V`): `W_sym·V + W_std·V + W_alt·V = V`, using the\nnormalisation `W_sym + W_std + W_alt = 1`.  Together with\n`a3_denominator` (`= 1 + W_std`) this gives `a₃ = V / (1 + W_std)`.\n\n(Corrected 2026-07-11: an earlier draft stated the right-hand side as\n`V·(1 + W_std)`, which is false — it would require `V·W_std = 0`. The\nnumerator of the equal-characters a₃ is `V`, the denominator\n`1 + W_std`; the quotient is `V/(1 + W_std)`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.a3_denominator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.a3_denominator","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L209-L219","doc":"The denominator of the a₃ formula is `1 + W_std`.\n\nFrom `W_sym + W_std + W_alt = 1` and `W_sym = W_alt`:\n`W_sym·1 + W_std·2 + W_alt·1 = W_sym + W_alt + 2W_std\n= (1 - W_std) + 2W_std = 1 + W_std`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.det_two_T_pn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.det_two_T_pn","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L203-L205","doc":"For the pn crossing, `det(2·T_pn) = -HA² - 4 = -(HA² + 4)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.det_T_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.det_T_nn","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L199-L201","doc":"det(T_nn) = det([[0, 1], [1, -HA]]) = -1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.det_T_pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.det_T_pp","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L196-L197","doc":"det(T_pp) = det([[HA, 1], [1, 0]]) = -1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.pp_nn_extremal_cancel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.pp_nn_extremal_cancel","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L185-L192","doc":"For pp crossings the extremal contribution is `+2w·HA` and for nn it\nis `-2w·HA`; the SUM pp + nn cancels exactly.  This is why Z=N nuclei\npreserve Frobenius stability. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.pn_extremal_contribution_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.pn_extremal_contribution_zero","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L177-L183","doc":"The extremal contribution of a pn crossing is zero: pn binding does\nNOT change the confinement (Frobenius) channels — it operates only in\nthe standard (binding) channel.  `P_ext(V_pn) = 0` by\n`extremal_cancellation`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.pn_volume_std_only","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.pn_volume_std_only","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L164-L173","doc":"For the pn crossing (`c=1`, midpoint `dh`) with `W_sym = W_alt`:\n`V_pn = W_std · (z + dh)` (`= W_std · (z - HA/2)`).\n\nThe symmetric and alternating contributions cancel by\n`extremal_cancellation`, leaving only the standard channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.crossing_deviation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.crossing_deviation","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L153-L160","doc":"The deviation `δV = V_pp - V_pn = W_sym · HA + W_std · (HA/2)`.  Written\nwith the pn midpoint `dh` (`HA/2 = -dh`): `δV = w · HA - w_std · dh`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.crossing_balance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.crossing_balance","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L142-L151","doc":"`V_pp + V_nn = 2 · V_pn` when `W_sym = W_alt` and the pn midpoint\n`dh + dh = -HA` holds.  This is the crossing-balance identity: the\n`q`-parts of pp and nn combine to `w_std·(2z - HA)`, matched by\n`2·V_pn`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.crossing_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.crossing_volume","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L134-L140","doc":"Single-crossing Wedderburn volume for crossing type (c, d).\n\nV(c, d) = W_sym · (c·q + d) + W_std · (z·c + d) + W_alt · (-c·q⁻¹ + d)\n\nFor pp: (c=1, d=0); for nn: (c=1, d=-HA); for pn: (c=1, d=-HA/2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.weighted_extremal_cancellation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.weighted_extremal_cancellation","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L126-L130","doc":"Since `W_sym = W_alt`, the weighted sum also vanishes:\n`W_sym · χ_sym + W_alt · χ_alt = W_sym · (χ_sym + χ_alt) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.extremal_cancellation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.extremal_cancellation","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L116-L124","doc":"For the pn crossing with `d + d = -(c · HA)` (i.e. `d = -c·HA/2`), the\nsum `χ_sym + χ_alt = 0`.\n\nProof: `χ_sym + χ_alt = (c·q + d) + (-c·q⁻¹ + d) = c·(q - q⁻¹) + 2d\n= c·HA + 2d = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.chi_alt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.chi_alt","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L109-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.chi_sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.chi_sym","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L105-L108","doc":"For a crossing with parameters (c, d):\nχ_sym(c, d) = c·q + d\nχ_alt(c, d) = -c·q⁻¹ + d ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.HA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.HA","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L102-L103","doc":"The Hecke parameter HA = q - q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.alt_eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.alt_eigenvalue","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L99-L100","doc":"Eigenvalue of σ in the alternating (dim-1) rep: λ_alt = -q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.sym_eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.sym_eigenvalue","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L96-L97","doc":"Eigenvalue of σ in the symmetric (dim-1) rep: λ_sym = q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.dq_sym_sq_eq_dq_alt_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.dq_sym_sq_eq_dq_alt_sq","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L84-L92","doc":"**Equality of the symmetric/alternating Wedderburn numerators**:\n`d_q((3))² = d_q((1,1,1))²` in `R_q`.\n\nThe Wedderburn weight is `W_λ = d_q(λ)² / [3]!`.  Both channels share\nthe common `[3]!` denominator, so `W_sym = W_alt` is *equivalent* to\nthis numerator equality — and both hook-products equal `[3]_q!`\n(`dq_sym_eq_one`, `dq_alt_eq_one`), so the numerators coincide. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.dq_alt_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.dq_alt_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L78-L82","doc":"**The q-dimension of the alternating rep `(1,1,1)` is `1`** — `(1,1,1)`\nis the transpose of `(3)`, so its hook multiset `{3,2,1}` is identical;\n`hooksAlt` is definitionally `hooksSym`, so this is exactly\n`dq_sym_eq_one` (Gemini review). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.dq_sym_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.dq_sym_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L70-L76","doc":"**The q-dimension of the symmetric rep `(3)` is `1`.**  Stated over the\n`CommRing` `R_q` (no division) as the numerator/denominator identity\n`∏_{h ∈ hooks}[h]_q = [3]_q!`, i.e. `d_q((3)) = [3]_q!/∏hooks = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.qFactorial3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.qFactorial3","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L67-L68","doc":"`[3]_q! = [3]_q · [2]_q · [1]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.hooksAlt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.hooksAlt","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L62-L65","doc":"Hook lengths of the alternating partition `(1,1,1)` (a single column):\nthe cell `(i, 1)` has arm `0`, leg `3 - i`, hook `0 + (3 - i) + 1` —\ngiving `{3, 2, 1}` (the transpose of `(3)`; identical multiset). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.hooksSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.hooksSym","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L57-L60","doc":"Hook lengths of the symmetric partition `(3)` (a single row): the cell\n`(1, j)` has arm `3 - j`, leg `0`, hook `(3 - j) + 0 + 1` — giving\n`{3, 2, 1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.qHookProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.qHookProd","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ConfinedKnotBinding.lean#L54-L55","doc":"The balanced-q hook product `∏_{h ∈ hooks} [h]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}